+// Original Fortnite 12.60 cooked instanced static mesh components (unversioned packages) predate the per-instance
+// custom data layout: they serialize no PerInstanceSMCustomData bulk array, and the cooked FStaticMeshInstanceData
+// carries neither NumCustomDataFloats nor the InstanceCustomData buffer (byte-level evidence from
+// Athena_Tutorial_Map_A FoliageInstancedStaticMeshComponent: bCooked, PerInstanceSMData(64,11), u64 RenderDataSize=560 =
+// 4+4+(8+16*11)+(8+24*11)+(8+8*11), then the HISM cluster tree). Unversioned packages report the newest custom
+// versions, so the stock PerInstanceCustomData gates would read the newer layout. Same default-on gate and opt-out
+// (-FortniteNoLegacyStaticMesh) as the static mesh layout. See porting/patches/ue425-legacy-ism-layout.patch.
+static bool FortniteUseLegacyInstancedMeshLayout(FArchive& Ar)
+{
+	extern bool FortniteUseLegacyStaticMeshLayout(FArchive& Ar);
+	return Ar.IsLoading() && FortniteUseLegacyStaticMeshLayout(Ar);
+}
